  "title": "Lantern Strait",
  "rules": [
    "Upper crossing (4,2) is always open; lower crossing (4,4) is open at tide phases 0..3 and closed at phases 4..7.",
    "Adjacent EAST/WEST requests set public lanterns and seek a three-step entrance lease. Matching side and rotating initiative decide conflicts before movement.",
    "Unreserved entrances are open to either direction. A lease excludes other entrants; YIELD releases it and departure from the gate also releases it.",
    "Maneuvers and signals each spend one fuel, including blocked attempts. A grounded vessel must wait for the tide; exhausted vessels remain physical obstacles.",
    "Only own destination is private. Docking exactly there starts two later steps of service; completed vessels depart and release their berth.",
    "Own completion is worth 0.75 plus 0.25 shared per completion; working cost is 1/64 per step, collision cost 1/8, new stranding cost 1/2."
  ],
